: OpenAI Responses API stream (POST /responses, store=false,
: include=["reasoning.encrypted_content"]) as the ChatGPT subscription
: endpoint at chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex serves it.
:
: A two-call PARALLEL BATCH, both calls naming the SAME tool. The reasoning
: item leads, because that is the order the endpoint emits in and the order
: build_input has to replay in; its encrypted_content is opaque and is the
: only thing that stops a store=false reasoning model deriving its whole
: chain of thought again on the next step, and being billed for it again.
:
: Same-tool is the case the whole call_id change exists for. Correlating a
: result back to its call by tool name has two answers here and picks one,
: which feeds the model file a.rs's contents as the answer to the read of
: b.rs. Only call_a and call_b tell the two apart, and the ids in this fixture
: are the only place a test can get them without inventing them.
:
: usage.input_tokens_details.cached_tokens is a subset of input_tokens, the
: way OpenAI counts everywhere, and is never added to it.
:
: Lines starting with a colon are SSE comments. The adapter skips every line
: that does not begin with "data" plus a colon, so this header and the event:
: lines travel with the bytes without changing what is parsed.
:
: Transcribed from the shape chatgpt::tests::
: a_two_call_batch_from_the_wire_keeps_both_ids_apart asserts. See the header
: of tests/recorded_provider.rs for how to re-record it from a live stream
: once the adapter's dump hook exists.

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_1","encrypted_content":"gAAAAAB-opaque","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"read both"}]}}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call","name":"read_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"a.rs\"}","call_id":"call_a"}}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call","name":"read_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"b.rs\"}","call_id":"call_b"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","response":{"usage":{"input_tokens":48000,"output_tokens":120,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":46080}}}}
